From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:49:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] editor: a Markdown quote continues on a new line and on a
 paste

Operator, 2026-11-22: the `>` quote "works on one line only; it should
extend as I break lines or paste several". Upstream continues `- ` and
`1. ` lists on a newline (list_delimiter_for_newline) but not quotes, and
its own test_markdown_indents case 7 pinned that: after "> Item 1" the
new line began bare, and a pasted paragraph left the quote after its
first line. The agent composer is a Markdown buffer, so it had the same
gap, and 0107's quote look ended with the markers.

markdown_quote.rs (new, pure functions, then two small hooks):
- Editor::newline, after the list step and under the same
  extend_list_on_newline setting, in a Markdown buffer: in the quoted
  text of a quote line the new line starts with the quote's markers,
  normalised to "> " per level; on an empty quote line one level ends
  ("> > " becomes "> ", "> " becomes empty), as an empty list item ends
  a list. Inside the markers a newline stays plain.
- edit_for_markdown_paste (upstream's Markdown paste hook): a multi-line
  paste into the quoted text of a quote line gets the markers after each
  of its newlines. A one-line paste and a URL paste are unchanged.
CommonMark's lazy continuation would already read a bare next line as
quoted, but neither the composer's look nor a reader's eye does.
NewlineConfig became pub(crate) for the new step to set it; the quote
step reuses ClearCurrentLine and UnindentCurrentLine, the variants the
list step uses for the same purpose.

Tests: markdown_quote::tests, 3 unit and 3 on an EditorTestContext with
the Markdown grammar (newline continues and ends levels, nested quotes,
lists unchanged, a paste quoted, a paste outside a quote unchanged).
Upstream's test_markdown_indents case 7 now expects "> " on the new
line. Red seen with the newline step and the paste hook disabled: the
two editor tests and case 7 failed, the guard (newline outside a quote)
passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

